<title>USA: High Plains Wheat - Basis continues to edge higher.</title>
<headline>High Plains Wheat - Basis continues to edge higher.</headline>
<dateline>KANSAS CITY, Mo. 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hard red winter wheat basis bids continued an overall gentle upward trend on Wednesday, boosted by the continued lack of farmer selling, dealers said.</p>
<p>&quot;The basis is slowly working higher. Movement is still very, very slow,&quot; one Kansas dealer said.</p>
<p>Dealers said mills still needed to buy some old crop wheat but the recent decline in prices had brought farmer selling to a virtual halt. Many farmers remained preoccupied with planting spring crops such as corn, sorghum and soybeans.  </p>
